Fireworks public KV-outer
  https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/MSA/tree/fireworks-msa
  python/mbsa/cute/kvouter/ derives from the public
  python/fmha_sm100/kvouter/ modules. Index and schedule retain
  Fireworks AI Apache-2.0 headers; forward/combine retain BSD-3-Clause
  AND Apache-2.0 headers and FlashAttention-4 source attribution.
  Component license texts, AUTHORS and the original upstream NOTICE are
  retained under python/mbsa/third_party/fireworks/. MBSA adaptations include
  local imports, reusable caller-owned buffers, prepared launchers and
  rebinding, CUTLASS API/TMEM synchronization compatibility, paged-tail safety
  and live strided views. Optional scaled FP8 partial storage is an MBSA
  semantic adaptation: combination restores the recorded per-row scale.
  This publicly sourced backend includes compact selected-slot indexing
  and tile-ordered partials; these are independent of removed private
  implementations. Fixed and Dynamic outputs remain separate.
  Detailed source and adaptation records remain in the component
  PROVENANCE.md and UPSTREAM.json.

FlashAttention-4 public Fixed dependency and synchronization override
  https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention
  python/mbsa/cute/fixed_attention.py independently constructs exact Fixed
  block metadata and calls the installed flash-attn-4==4.0.0b20 wrapper.
  fixed_sync.py derives FlashAttentionForwardSm100.kernel from
  flash_attn/cute/flash_fwd_sm100.py, with
  converged TMEM synchronization, guarded configurations and a private JIT
  cache. MBSA adapts TMEM allocation/retirement, role synchronization and FP8
  row-maximum rescaling, while retaining the public softmax implementation
  through a private factory. Version, source-content and class-binding guards
  reject incompatible installed dependencies. BSD-3-Clause LICENSE and
  AUTHORS are retained under python/mbsa/third_party/fa4/. MBSA changes retain
  Apache-2.0 attribution. Fixed and Dynamic states remain separate.
  merge_vectorized.py is an original warp-owned/vector-copy implementation.
  The existing PROVENANCE.md and UPSTREAM.json in the FA4 license directory
  retain the public source snapshot and integration details.

