Maxwell Team host attention orchestration
  python/mbsa/cute/plan.py and python/mbsa/cute/prefill.py are Maxwell Team
  Apache-2.0 host code. plan.py defines the public planning, tensor metadata,
  validation and workspace contracts; prefill.py prepares and dispatches
  Fixed, Dynamic and Index work. Neither file contains a GPU kernel
  implementation. The default Blackwell path uses the separately attributed
  public FA4 Fixed backend, Fireworks Dynamic backend, MBSA Index router and
  the original merge_vectorized.py implementation.

MBSA integration
  Hopper uses its architecture-specific Fixed/Dynamic pipeline. The Blackwell
  default uses FA4 Fixed and Fireworks Dynamic, with independent output and
  LSE states.
  Native Index routing supports BF16, FP16 and FP8; native MXFP6 requires
  Blackwell. Optional FP8 partials use the scaled storage and combination
  adaptation described above.
  Installed runtime dependencies retain their own licenses. The independent
  FP32 correctness oracle is test support and is not shipped in the runtime.

